From: arch-xiaomi-sheng maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sheng: drop shared placeholder BD address

The address in the board DTS is a shared placeholder and is not the factory
Bluetooth identity stored in the device's persist partition.  A fixed public
address also causes collisions between devices.

Remove it from the generic board description.  Platform firmware or the boot
image builder must inject the per-device local-bd-address property.

Signed-off-by: arch-xiaomi-sheng maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550-xiaomi-sheng.dts | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550-xiaomi-sheng.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550-xiaomi-sheng.dts
index 6251be81b931..6cade6d0d8aa 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550-xiaomi-sheng.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550-xiaomi-sheng.dts
@@ -1746,8 +1746,6 @@ &uart14 {
 	bluetooth {
 		compatible = "qcom,wcn7850-bt";
 
-		local-bd-address = [ 24 00 00 00 5a ad ];
-
 		vddrfacmn-supply = <&vreg_pmu_rfa_cmn>;
 		vddaon-supply = <&vreg_pmu_aon_0p59>;
 		vddwlcx-supply = <&vreg_pmu_wlcx_0p8>;
-- 
2.51.0
